7a3b5cc8526adf04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rishabhchheda01/canvas-lms/commits/fb36281b0e64fdaaff7a43d97a3b5cc8526adf04"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rishabhchheda01/canvas-lms/commits/988428d99f6dfb3905af40326cb518aa585365af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-05T14:53:14Z","email":"hannah.roach@instructure.com","name":"Hannah Roach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-09T16:26:48Z","email":"hannah.roach@instructure.com","name":"Hannah Roach"},"message":"update course import text\n\nUpdate the course import text to read \"The security\nparameters for the external tool <tool_name> may need\nto be set in Course Settings.\"\n\nfixes LX-2627\nflag=none\n\ntest plan:\n1. create two courses\n2. navigate to app settings of one course\n3. add the Redirect Tool app\n4. export the course\n5. in the other course created, open Course\nImport Tools in settings\n6. select \"Canvas course export package\" and upload\nthe imscc file of the first course\n7. select \"All content\"\n8. import the imscc file\n9. on the \"Content imports\" table, under \"Action\",\nclick on \"View Issues\"\n10. Observe that the warning reads \"The security\nparameters for the external tool \"Redirect Tool\"\nmay need to be set in Course Settings.\"\n\nChange-Id: I196f3fabeb98638ef647f9577ced17f1723634b7\nReviewed-on: https://gerrit.instructure.com/c/canvas-lms/+/380594\nTested-by: Service Cloud Jenkins <svc.cloudjenkins@instructure.com>\nReviewed-by: Jaime Lozano <jaime.lozano@instructure.com>\nQA-Review: Jaime Lozano <jaime.lozano@instructure.com>\nProduct-Review: Jaime Lozano <jaime.lozano@instructure.com>","tree":{"sha":"688dfac403e93b36ef2565a04d7972f5e9468fb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rishabhchheda01/canvas-lms/git/trees/688dfac403e93b36ef2565a04d7972f5e9468fb3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rishabhchheda01/canvas-lms/git/commits/988428d99f6dfb3905af40326cb518aa585365af","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rishabhchheda01/canvas-lms/commit/988428d99f6dfb3905af40326cb518aa585365af","node_id":"C_kwDOO9V729oAKDk4ODQyOGQ5OWY2ZGZiMzkwNWFmNDAzMjZjYjUxOGFhNTg1MzY1YWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rishabhchheda01/canvas-lms/commit/2d49031e1b55307a4c6a7a1adb2b24ff33ef70f2","sha":"2d49031e1b55307a4c6a7a1adb2b24ff33ef70f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rishabhchheda01/canvas-lms/commits/2d49031e1b55307a4c6a7a1adb2b24ff33ef70f2"}],"sha":"988428d99f6dfb3905af40326cb518aa585365af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rishabhchheda01/canvas-lms/commits/988428d99f6dfb3905af40326cb518aa585365af"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rishabhchheda01/canvas-lms/commits/2d49031e1b55307a4c6a7a1adb2b24ff33ef70f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-02T07:07:13Z","email":"jason.perry@instructure.com","name":"Jason Perry"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-09T15:44:27Z","email":"jason.perry@instructure.com","name":"Jason Perry"},"message":"Don''t add empty scope when no scope is inferred\n\nIn some cases, like STI models, the scope is not inferred correctly,\nand it results in an empty scope \"\" being added to the translation key.\nThis also results in some keys being duplicated in the i18n extraction,\nwhich has led to conflicting translations.\n\nFixes FOO-5269\nflag=none\n\nTest plan:\n- Run the i18n extraction (bundle exec rake i18n:extract) and see keys\n  like `submission_types.a_file_upload` are not extract with an empty\n  string ('''') for a top level scope, as well as duplicated any longer.\n\nChange-Id: I50dbb759163a801471d72a15528101af07ba7f35\nReviewed-on: https://gerrit.instructure.com/c/canvas-lms/+/379813\nReviewed-by: Adrián Grúber <adrian.gruber@instructure.com>\nReviewed-by: August Thornton <august@instructure.com>\nReviewed-by: Charley Kline <ckline@instructure.com>\nReviewed-by: Ryan Norton <rnorton@i